b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), recursive procedures and function designators with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values, and problems/13-deterministic-scale.md, Representation), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: k, the first place of range(k, n, s). n is the instance's size, from the instance line;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P13d, prescribed. range(k, n, s) and revacc(s, r), in that order. range computes s from k and n by its cases, in order, as a function, the direction the query uses. Case 1: range(m, n, the empty sequence) if m is greater than n. Case 2: range(m, n, the sequence of m alone ++ t) if m is at most n and range(m + 1, n, t). revacc computes r from s by its one case: revacc(a, b) if racc(a, the empty sequence, b). racc computes its third place from the first two by its cases, in order. Case 1: racc(the empty sequence, b, b). Case 2: racc(the sequence of h alone ++ t, c, b) if racc(t, the sequence of h alone ++ c, b). A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence of hd[c] alone ++ the sequence tl[c], so that taking the tail is the one subscript tl[c], in constant time. range makes L cells for its L elements and racc L more, and the store is sized from k and n;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, lo, len, size;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constant;
  lo := read;
  len := i̲f̲ lo > n t̲h̲e̲n̲ 0 e̲l̲s̲e̲ n - lo + 1;
  size := len + len + 1;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ top, s0, r0, range1, range2, revacc1, racc1, racc2;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl[1:size];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence of h alone ++ the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ range(m, n);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ m, n; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ m, n;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ range(m, n, s), computing s by its cases, in order;
  i̲f̲ m > n t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ range1 := range1 + 1; range := 0 e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ t;
    range2 := range2 + 1;
    t := range(m + 1, n);
    range := cons(m, t)
  e̲n̲d̲ range;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ racc(a, c);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a, c; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, c;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ racc(a, c, b), computing b by its cases, in order;
  i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ racc1 := racc1 + 1; racc := c e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    racc2 := racc2 + 1;
    racc := racc(tl[a], cons(hd[a], c))
  e̲n̲d̲ racc;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ revacc(a);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ revacc(a, b), computing b by its one case;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    revacc1 := revacc1 + 1;
    revacc := racc(a, 0)
  e̲n̲d̲ revacc;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(p);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence, its elements in parentheses, separated by commas, with a new line after every ten elements so that no line of the X1 passes its 144 positions;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, c;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    c := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ p ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      num(hd[p]); p := tl[p]; c := c + 1;
      i̲f̲ p ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      i̲f̲ c = 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ NLCR; c := 0 e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

  top := range1 := range2 := revacc1 := racc1 := racc2 := 0;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the query: range(k, n, s) and revacc(s, r), in that order;
  s0 := range(lo, n);
  r0 := revacc(s0);

  PRINTTEXT(`[answer]s = '); printseq(s0); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`,'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲; PRINTTEXT(`r = '); printseq(r0); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the applications of each case, and the store held after the answer;
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  PRINTTEXT(`cells held after the answer: '); num(top); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, the cells of s and r, none given back'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations range/1 '); num(range1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations range/2 '); num(range2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations revacc/1 '); num(revacc1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations racc/1 '); num(racc1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations racc/2 '); num(racc2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
